-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), piece cr1 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: the individual to whom the Regulations are applied -- a worker (an employee), a self-employed person,
-- the person who runs a small business and has employees, a legal representative of a person who has died,
-- a person who owes or is owed interest. The benefits the Act pays (retirement, disability, survivor's, children's)
-- are not in this piece's ranges (they belong to the Act's Part II and to the Regulations' Part V): the questions
-- here are the contribution, pensionable-employment, return, interest, election and Social Insurance Number
-- questions.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules of the layer-1 modules imported above as the questions that person asks, and takes
-- plain inputs: yes/no, a number, a date, or one of the modules' own choices, each with an @desc worded as the
-- person would be asked. The records the layer-1 rules expect are built inside each question, in its WHERE,
-- from those answers, and the SAME layer-1 rule is then called; no rule is restated. A record field that the rule
-- called never reads is given a fixed placeholder, with a comment saying so.
--
-- THE FIGURES THE ACT FIXES (the contribution rates, the basic exemption, the maximum pensionable earnings) are
-- section 11.1/11.2, 17 to 20 matters of the Act, outside this piece's ranges (piece cp1). The person cannot
-- state them from memory, so each question that needs them asks for them as published for the year, and says
-- which section of the Act fixes them. A merged seat should take them from the Act's rules instead.
--
-- THE ACT'S OWN JUDGMENTS that these Regulations hand to someone else (the Minister's satisfaction, the Minister's
-- approval of a basis, the President of the Treasury Board's wish, a reasonable time) are asked as facts about that
-- other person's decision ("Has the Minister approved ...?"), never decided here.
--
-- Where a question answers MAYBE: NOTHING means the Regulations do not decide that case, never "no" or "nil".
--
-- Choices assumed, not ruled: (1) the full pay-deduction question and a short one are both offered; (2) regulation
-- 8(1.1)(b), (1.12), (1.13) and 8.2 (the days that are not Saturdays or holidays, and an employer's history of
-- remitting) stay in layer 1 only, and the seat asks regulation 8(1) and 8(2); (3) a few questions are phrased as
-- "Must I ..." by a person who runs a business and has employees (regulation 11), beside the employee's own "Must
-- my employer ...".

§ `Canada Pension Plan Regulations -- the individual's questions`

§§ `A. What comes off my pay, and what my employer adds (regs 3 to 7)`

-- Regs 4, 5, 5.1, 6 (with 3). The amount an employer deducts from one payment: base and first additional
-- contributions by regulation 5 (rounded to the cent, never above the year's limit), the second additional by 5.1
-- from 2024, both reduced by what a provincial pension plan has already taken (regulation 6). NOTHING where the
-- provincial plan's rates are nil or the year is before 2024 for the second additional part with no first part.
@export How much will my employer deduct from this pay for the Canada Pension Plan (regs 3 to 7)?
GIVEN `the year of this pay` IS A NUMBER @desc In which calendar year is this pay paid (for example 2026)?
      `the contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the contribution rate for employees for that year under section 11.1 of the Act, as a fraction (1 per cent is 0.01)?
      `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional contribution rate for employees for that year under section 11.2 of the Act, as a fraction (0 if there is none for the year)?
      `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second additional contribution rate for employees for that year under section 11.2 of the Act, as a fraction (0 if there is none for the year)?
      `the basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the basic exemption for that year under sections 19 and 20 of the Act, in dollars?
      `the maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the maximum pensionable earnings for that year under section 18 of the Act, in dollars?
      `the additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the additional maximum pensionable earnings for that year under section 18.1 of the Act, in dollars?
      `the amount of this pay from pensionable employment` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is this pay (the whole payment from your pensionable employment), in dollars?
      `the part of this pay that is ordinary remuneration` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of this pay is ordinary remuneration (pay for the pay period paid on the pay day, or a director's fees where the corporation pays no other remuneration), in dollars?
      `how I am ordinarily paid` IS A `cr1 How an employee is ordinarily paid` @desc How are you ordinarily paid (hourly, daily, weekly, bi-weekly, and so on, or in some other way)?
      `the number of days in my pay period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days are in your pay period? (Only used if you are paid in some other way; otherwise any number.)
      `the number of pay periods ending in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pay periods end in the year (26 or 27 if you are paid bi-weekly, 52 or 53 if weekly)?
      `base and first additional contributions already deducted this year` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the base and first additional contributions has this employer already deducted from your pay this year, in dollars?
      `second additional contributions already deducted this year` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the second additional contribution has this employer already deducted from your pay this year, in dollars?
      `the total pay already paid to me this year by this employer` IS A NUMBER @desc How much remuneration has this employer already paid you this year, before this pay, in dollars?
      `I made contributions this year under a provincial pension plan on pay from this employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made base and first additional contributions this year under a provincial pension plan on pay from this employer?
      `base and first additional contributions already required under the provincial plan` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the base and first additional contributions has this employer already been required to deduct under the provincial pension plan this year, in dollars?
      `second additional contributions already required under the provincial plan` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the second additional contribution has this employer already been required to deduct under the provincial pension plan this year, in dollars?
      `the sum of the provincial plan's contribution rate and first additional rate for employees` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the sum of the provincial plan's contribution rate and first additional contribution rate for employees, as a fraction?
      `the provincial plan's second additional rate for employees` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the provincial plan's second additional contribution rate for employees, as a fraction?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much will my employer deduct from this pay for the Canada Pension Plan` IS
    `reg 4 — the employee's contribution to deduct from a payment` `the year of this pay` `the Act's figures` `this pay` `my deductions so far` `my provincial plan position`
    WHERE
        `the Act's figures` MEANS `cr1 Figures the Act sets for a year` WITH
            `the contribution rate for employees` IS `the contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the first additional contribution rate for employees` IS `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the second additional contribution rate for employees` IS `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the basic exemption` IS `the basic exemption for the year`
            `the maximum pensionable earnings` IS `the maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
            `the additional maximum pensionable earnings` IS `the additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
        `this pay` MEANS `cr1 Payment of remuneration` WITH
            `the payment of remuneration from pensionable employment` IS `the amount of this pay from pensionable employment`
            `the part of the payment that is ordinary remuneration` IS `the part of this pay that is ordinary remuneration`
            `how the employee is ordinarily paid` IS `how I am ordinarily paid`
            `the number of days in the pay period` IS `the number of days in my pay period`
            `the number of pay periods ending in the year` IS `the number of pay periods ending in the year`
        `my deductions so far` MEANS `cr1 Position earlier in the year` WITH
            `base and first additional contributions already deducted under this Part` IS `base and first additional contributions already deducted this year`
            `second additional contributions already deducted under this Part` IS `second additional contributions already deducted this year`
            `total remuneration the employer has already paid the employee in the year` IS `the total pay already paid to me this year by this employer`
        `my provincial plan position` MEANS `cr1 Provincial pension plan position` WITH
            `the employee has made contributions for the year under a provincial pension plan in respect of salary and wages paid by the employer` IS `I made contributions this year under a provincial pension plan on pay from this employer`
            `base and first additional contributions already required to be deducted under the provincial pension plan` IS `base and first additional contributions already required under the provincial plan`
            `second additional contributions already required to be deducted under the provincial pension plan` IS `second additional contributions already required under the provincial plan`
            `sum of the provincial plan's contribution rate and first additional contribution rate for employees` IS `the sum of the provincial plan's contribution rate and first additional rate for employees`
            `the provincial plan's second additional contribution rate for employees` IS `the provincial plan's second additional rate for employees`

-- The short form of the question: no earlier deductions this year, no provincial plan, the second additional
-- contribution not asked (assumed, not ruled: the common case of an employee's first pay). Placeholders: the
-- second additional rate, the additional maximum pensionable earnings and the earlier totals are not read by
-- regulation 5.
@export How much will my employer deduct from this pay for the base and first additional contributions, if nothing has yet been deducted this year (regs 4 and 5)?
GIVEN `the contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the contribution rate for employees for the year under section 11.1 of the Act, as a fraction (1 per cent is 0.01)?
      `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year under section 11.2 of the Act, as a fraction (0 if there is none for the year)?
      `the basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the basic exemption for the year under sections 19 and 20 of the Act, in dollars?
      `the maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the maximum pensionable earnings for the year under section 18 of the Act, in dollars?
      `the amount of this pay from pensionable employment` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is this pay (the whole payment from your pensionable employment), in dollars?
      `the part of this pay that is ordinary remuneration` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of this pay is ordinary remuneration, in dollars?
      `how I am ordinarily paid` IS A `cr1 How an employee is ordinarily paid` @desc How are you ordinarily paid (hourly, daily, weekly, bi-weekly, and so on, or in some other way)?
      `the number of days in my pay period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days are in your pay period? (Only used if you are paid in some other way; otherwise any number.)
      `the number of pay periods ending in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pay periods end in the year (26 or 27 if you are paid bi-weekly, 52 or 53 if weekly)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much will my employer deduct from this pay for the base and first additional contributions if nothing has yet been deducted this year` IS
    `reg 5 — the base and first additional contributions to deduct from a payment` `the Act's figures` `this pay` `nothing deducted yet` `no provincial plan`
    WHERE
        `the Act's figures` MEANS `cr1 Figures the Act sets for a year` WITH
            `the contribution rate for employees` IS `the contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the first additional contribution rate for employees` IS `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year`
            -- Placeholders: regulation 5 does not read the second additional rate or the additional maximum pensionable earnings.
            `the second additional contribution rate for employees` IS 0
            `the basic exemption` IS `the basic exemption for the year`
            `the maximum pensionable earnings` IS `the maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
            `the additional maximum pensionable earnings` IS 0
        `this pay` MEANS `cr1 Payment of remuneration` WITH
            `the payment of remuneration from pensionable employment` IS `the amount of this pay from pensionable employment`
            `the part of the payment that is ordinary remuneration` IS `the part of this pay that is ordinary remuneration`
            `how the employee is ordinarily paid` IS `how I am ordinarily paid`
            `the number of days in the pay period` IS `the number of days in my pay period`
            `the number of pay periods ending in the year` IS `the number of pay periods ending in the year`
        `nothing deducted yet` MEANS `cr1 Position earlier in the year` WITH
            `base and first additional contributions already deducted under this Part` IS 0
            -- Placeholders: regulation 5 does not read the second additional deductions or the year-to-date pay.
            `second additional contributions already deducted under this Part` IS 0
            `total remuneration the employer has already paid the employee in the year` IS 0
        `no provincial plan` MEANS `cr1 Provincial pension plan position` WITH
            `the employee has made contributions for the year under a provincial pension plan in respect of salary and wages paid by the employer` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholders: no provincial plan contributions are counted when the first field is FALSE.
            `base and first additional contributions already required to be deducted under the provincial pension plan` IS 0
            `second additional contributions already required to be deducted under the provincial pension plan` IS 0
            `sum of the provincial plan's contribution rate and first additional contribution rate for employees` IS 0
            `the provincial plan's second additional contribution rate for employees` IS 0

-- Reg 7 and the definition of "employer's contribution" in reg 3: the employer's own contribution equals what is
-- deducted from the employee. This is the employee's claim and the employer's duty in one rule.
@export How much must my employer add from its own money for each deduction from my pay (reg 7)?
GIVEN `the amount my employer is required to deduct from this pay under Part I of the Regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is your employer required to deduct from this pay for the Canada Pension Plan (all of the contributions), in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must my employer add from its own money for each deduction from my pay` IS
    `reg 7 — the employer's contribution to remit in respect of a payment` (JUST `the amount my employer is required to deduct from this pay under Part I of the Regulations`)

-- Reg 3 "year's maximum ... contribution": the most that can be deducted from one employee's pay in a year.
@export What is the most Canada Pension Plan contribution that can be deducted from my pay in a year (reg 3, reg 5(8), reg 5.1(3))?
GIVEN `the contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the contribution rate for employees for the year under section 11.1 of the Act, as a fraction (1 per cent is 0.01)?
      `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year under section 11.2 of the Act, as a fraction (0 if there is none)?
      `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year under section 11.2 of the Act, as a fraction (0 if there is none)?
      `the basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the basic exemption for the year under sections 19 and 20 of the Act, in dollars?
      `the maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the maximum pensionable earnings for the year under section 18 of the Act, in dollars?
      `the additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year under section 18.1 of the Act, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most Canada Pension Plan contribution that can be deducted from my pay in a year` IS
    (`reg 3 — the year's maximum base contribution` `the Act's figures`)
    PLUS (`reg 3 — the year's maximum first additional contribution` `the Act's figures`)
    PLUS (`reg 3 — the year's maximum second additional contribution` `the Act's figures`)
    WHERE
        `the Act's figures` MEANS `cr1 Figures the Act sets for a year` WITH
            `the contribution rate for employees` IS `the contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the first additional contribution rate for employees` IS `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the second additional contribution rate for employees` IS `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the basic exemption` IS `the basic exemption for the year`
            `the maximum pensionable earnings` IS `the maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
            `the additional maximum pensionable earnings` IS `the additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year`

-- Reg 5(5): the basic exemption for each pay period.
@export What is my basic exemption for each pay period (reg 5(5))?
GIVEN `how I am ordinarily paid` IS A `cr1 How an employee is ordinarily paid` @desc How are you ordinarily paid (hourly, daily, weekly, bi-weekly, and so on, or in some other way)?
      `the number of days in my pay period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days are in your pay period? (Only used if you are paid in some other way; otherwise any number.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my basic exemption for each pay period` IS
    `reg 5(5) — the employee's basic exemption for a pay period` `how I am ordinarily paid` `the number of days in my pay period`

-- Reg 3 "ordinary remuneration".
@export Is this pay ordinary remuneration for the Canada Pension Plan (reg 3)?
GIVEN `this is remuneration paid to me on a pay day in respect of my employment in the relevant pay period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this remuneration paid to you on a pay day in respect of your employment in the relevant pay period?
      `this is fees paid to me as a director of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this fees paid to you as a director of a corporation?
      `the corporation pays me no other remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation pay you no other remuneration?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this pay ordinary remuneration for the Canada Pension Plan` IF
    `reg 3 — a payment is ordinary remuneration` `this is remuneration paid to me on a pay day in respect of my employment in the relevant pay period` `this is fees paid to me as a director of a corporation` `the corporation pays me no other remuneration`

-- Reg 6.1: the salary and wages a provincial plan's contributions stand for, used for the Act's sections 10 and 13.
@export How much of my pay counts as already contributed on for the base contribution under a provincial pension plan (reg 6.1(1))?
GIVEN `the base contributions I was required to make this year under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc How much in base contributions were you required to make this year under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
      `the base contribution rate for employees under the provincial plan for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the base contribution rate for employees under the provincial plan for the year, as a fraction?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my pay counts as already contributed on for the base contribution under a provincial pension plan` IS
    `reg 6.1(1) — the salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made under a provincial pension plan` `the base contributions I was required to make this year under a provincial pension plan` `the base contribution rate for employees under the provincial plan for the year`

@export How much of my pay counts as already contributed on for the first additional contribution under a provincial pension plan (reg 6.1(2))?
GIVEN `the first additional contributions I was required to make this year under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc How much in first additional contributions were you required to make this year under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
      `the first additional contribution rate for employees under the provincial pension plan for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional contribution rate for employees under the provincial plan for the year, as a fraction?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my pay counts as already contributed on for the first additional contribution under a provincial pension plan` IS
    `reg 6.1(2) — the salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made under a provincial pension plan` `the first additional contributions I was required to make this year under a provincial pension plan` `the first additional contribution rate for employees under the provincial pension plan for the year`

@export How much of my pay counts as already contributed on for the second additional contribution under a provincial pension plan (reg 6.1(3))?
GIVEN `the second additional contributions I was required to make this year under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc How much in second additional contributions were you required to make this year under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
      `the second additional contribution rate for employees under the provincial pension plan for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second additional contribution rate for employees under the provincial plan for the year, as a fraction?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my pay counts as already contributed on for the second additional contribution under a provincial pension plan` IS
    `reg 6.1(3) — the salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made under a provincial pension plan` `the second additional contributions I was required to make this year under a provincial pension plan` `the second additional contribution rate for employees under the provincial pension plan for the year`

-- Helper for the seat's questions: a person states a day only if the event has happened, so each optional day is
-- asked as a yes/no and a date. NOTHING when it has not happened. Not a provision.
GIVEN happened IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`cr1 seat: a day if it has happened` happened day MEANS
    IF happened THEN JUST day ELSE NOTHING


§§ `B. When my employer must remit, and who is treated as my employer (regs 8 to 8.3)`

-- Regulation 8(1.1)(b) counts days that are not Saturdays or holidays, and 8(1.12), (1.13) and 8.2 turn on an employer's
-- history of remitting. They are the employer's duties to the Receiver General, not a claim the worker holds, so this layer
-- asks only the monthly rule (reg 8(1)), the cessation rule (reg 8(2)) and the questions about what the worker is owed or can
-- check. The rest stay in the layer-1 modules.
@export By what day must my employer remit what it took from this pay, if it remits monthly (reg 8(1))?
GIVEN `the day my employer paid me this pay` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your employer pay you this remuneration?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must my employer remit what it took from this pay if it remits monthly` IS
    `reg 8(1) — the day by which contributions must be remitted` `the day my employer paid me this pay`

@export Were the contributions taken from my pay remitted on time (reg 8(1))?
GIVEN `the day the contributions were remitted` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the contributions remitted to the Receiver General?
      `the day by which they had to be remitted` IS A DATE @desc What was the day by which they had to be remitted?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Were the contributions taken from my pay remitted on time` IF
    `reg 8(1) — the contributions were remitted on time` `the day the contributions were remitted` `the day by which they had to be remitted`

@export My employer has stopped carrying on its business: by what day must it remit (reg 8(2))?
GIVEN `the day my employer ceased to carry on the business or activity` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your employer cease to carry on the business or activity?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `My employer has stopped carrying on its business so by what day must it remit` IS
    `reg 8(2) — the day by which an employer who ceases to carry on a business must remit` `the day my employer ceased to carry on the business or activity`

@export Does my employer's payment come with a return in the prescribed form (reg 8(3))?
GIVEN `a return accompanies the payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a return accompany your employer's payment to the Receiver General?
      `the return is on a form the Minister has authorized` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the return on a form the Minister has authorized?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my employer's payment come with a return in the prescribed form` IF
    `reg 8(3) — the payment is accompanied by a return in prescribed form` `a return accompanies the payment` `the return is on a form the Minister has authorized`

@export Is the person who pays my wages treated as my employer (reg 8.1(1))?
GIVEN `the person pays the remuneration of the employee wholly or in part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this person pay your remuneration wholly or in part?
      `the remuneration is in respect of pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the remuneration for pensionable employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the person who pays my wages treated as my employer` IF
    `reg 8.1(1) — a person is deemed to be an employer of an employee` `the person pays the remuneration of the employee wholly or in part` `the remuneration is in respect of pensionable employment`

@export How much can the person treated as my employer recover from my actual employer (reg 8.1(1.1))?
GIVEN `the person is deemed to be an employer under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who paid treated as your employer under regulation 8.1(1)?
      `the amount of the contributions the person has paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much in contributions has the person paid, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much can the person treated as my employer recover from my actual employer` IS
    `reg 8.1(1.1) — the amount the person may recover from the actual employer` `the person is deemed to be an employer under subsection (1)` `the amount of the contributions the person has paid`

@export If that person fails to pay, deduct or remit, does Part I of the Act apply to them as if they were my employer (reg 8.1(2))?
GIVEN `the person is deemed to be an employer under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who pays you treated as your employer under regulation 8.1(1)?
      `the person fails to pay, deduct or remit the contributions an employer is required to pay, deduct and remit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person fail to pay, deduct or remit the contributions an employer is required to pay, deduct and remit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `If the person treated as my employer fails to pay deduct or remit does Part I apply to them` IF
    `reg 8.1(2) — Part I of the Act applies to the person as if the actual employer` `the person is deemed to be an employer under subsection (1)` `the person fails to pay, deduct or remit the contributions an employer is required to pay, deduct and remit`

@export Is my mortgage a prescribed security interest (reg 8.3(1))?
GIVEN `the mortgage secures the performance of an obligation of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the mortgage secure the performance of an obligation of the person who owes the Receiver General?
      `the mortgage encumbers land or a building` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the mortgage encumber land or a building?
      `the mortgage was registered under the appropriate land registration system before the amount was deemed held in trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the mortgage registered under the appropriate land registration system before the amount was deemed held in trust?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my mortgage a prescribed security interest` IF
    `reg 8.3(1) — a mortgage is a prescribed security interest` `the mortgage secures the performance of an obligation of the person` `the mortgage encumbers land or a building` `the mortgage was registered under the appropriate land registration system before the amount was deemed held in trust`

@export How much can my prescribed security interest be (reg 8.3(2))?
GIVEN `the day of the failure to pay an amount deemed held in trust` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the person fail to pay an amount deemed held in trust?
      `an amount deemed to be held in trust remains unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an amount deemed to be held in trust remain unpaid?
      `the obligation outstanding at that time, secured by the mortgage` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the obligation secured by your mortgage was outstanding on that day, in dollars?
      `the value at the time of the failure of the secured creditor's other rights securing the obligation` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the value, on that day, of your other rights securing the obligation, in dollars?
      `the amounts applied after the failure on account of the obligation` IS A NUMBER @desc How much has been applied since that day on account of the obligation, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much can my prescribed security interest be` IS
    `reg 8.3(2) — the most the prescribed security interest may be` `the day of the failure to pay an amount deemed held in trust` `an amount deemed to be held in trust remains unpaid` `the obligation outstanding at that time, secured by the mortgage` `the value at the time of the failure of the secured creditor's other rights securing the obligation` `the amounts applied after the failure on account of the obligation`

@export Does a kind of interest that I hold count as part of a prescribed security interest (reg 8.3(3))?
GIVEN `the kind of interest I hold` IS A `cr1 Interest named in the avoidance-of-doubt clause on prescribed security interests` @desc Which kind of interest do you hold?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a kind of interest that I hold count as part of a prescribed security interest` IS
    `reg 8.3(3) — an interest is included in a prescribed security interest` `the kind of interest I hold`


§§ `C. Returns, my copies and the penalties for not giving them (regs 9 to 14)`

@export Must my employer file an information return for the year (reg 10(1))?
GIVEN `my employer has made a payment of remuneration during the year to an employee employed in pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employer paid remuneration during the year to an employee employed in pensionable employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer file an information return for the year` IF
    `reg 10(1) — the person must file an information return for the year` `my employer has made a payment of remuneration during the year to an employee employed in pensionable employment`

@export By what day must my employer file the information return for the year (reg 10)?
GIVEN `the year of the return` IS A NUMBER @desc For which calendar year is the return?
      `my employer has ceased to carry on the business or activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employer ceased to carry on the business or activity?
      `the day my employer ceased to carry on the business or activity` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your employer cease to carry on the business or activity? (Any date if it has not.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must my employer file the information return for the year` IS
    `reg 10 — the day by which the information return for a year must be filed` `the year of the return` (`cr1 seat: a day if it has happened` `my employer has ceased to carry on the business or activity` `the day my employer ceased to carry on the business or activity`)

@export Must I make an information return because the Minister has demanded it by registered letter (reg 11)?
GIVEN `I make or have made a payment of remuneration at any time to an employee employed in pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make, or have you made, a payment of remuneration at any time to an employee employed in pensionable employment?
      `the Minister has demanded the return by registered letter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister demanded the return by registered letter?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I make an information return because the Minister has demanded it by registered letter` IF
    `reg 11 — the person must make an information return on demand` `I make or have made a payment of remuneration at any time to an employee employed in pensionable employment` `the Minister has demanded the return by registered letter`

@export Did I file the return that was demanded in time (reg 11)?
GIVEN `the day I filed the return` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you file the return?
      `the day stipulated in the registered letter` IS A DATE @desc What day does the registered letter stipulate? (The Minister must be satisfied that it is a reasonable time.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I file the return that was demanded in time` IF
    `reg 11 — the return demanded was filed in time` `the day I filed the return` `the day stipulated in the registered letter`

@export A person has died: by what day must their legal representative file the return (reg 12(1))?
GIVEN `the day the person died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the person die?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `A person has died so by what day must their legal representative file the return` IS
    `reg 12(1) — the day by which the legal representatives must file the return` `the day the person died`

@export A person has died: what is the last day their return covers (reg 12(1))?
GIVEN `the year the return is required for` IS A NUMBER @desc For which calendar year is the return required?
      `the day the person died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the person die?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `A person has died so what is the last day their return covers` IS
    `reg 12(1) — the last day the return covers` `the year the return is required for` `the day the person died`

@export I deal with another person's property, business or estate: must I file their return for them (reg 12(2))?
GIVEN `the capacity in which I deal with the other person's property, business or estate` IS A `cr1 Capacity in which a person deals with another's property, business or estate` @desc In what capacity do you deal with the other person's property, business or estate (trustee in bankruptcy, assignee, liquidator, curator, receiver, trustee, committee, or another agent)?
      `the other person has not filed a return for the year as required by this Part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the other person not filed a return for the year as this Part requires?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I deal with another person's property business or estate so must I file their return for them` IF
    `reg 12(2) — the person must file the return on the other's behalf` `the capacity in which I deal with the other person's property, business or estate` `the other person has not filed a return for the year as required by this Part`

@export How many copies of my statement must my employer give me (reg 13)?
GIVEN `my employer is required by section 10 or 12 to file an information return for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer required by section 10 or 12 to file an information return for the year?
      `my employer gives me my portion in an electronic format` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer giving you your portion in an electronic format?
      `my employer may give me my portion in an electronic format` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May your employer give you your portion in an electronic format (see the next question)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many copies of my statement must my employer give me` IS
    `reg 13 — the number of copies the employee must be given` `my employer is required by section 10 or 12 to file an information return for the year` `my employer gives me my portion in an electronic format` `my employer may give me my portion in an electronic format`

@export Were my copies given to me the way and by the day required (reg 13(2))?
GIVEN `the copies were sent by mail to my latest known address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the copies sent by mail to your latest known address?
      `the copies were delivered to me in person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the copies delivered to you in person?
      `the day the copies were sent or delivered` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the copies sent or delivered?
      `the day my employer's return is required to be filed with the Minister` IS A DATE @desc On what day is your employer's return required to be filed with the Minister?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Were my copies given to me the way and by the day required` IF
    `reg 13(2) — the copies were supplied in the way and by the day required` `the copies were sent by mail to my latest known address` `the copies were delivered to me in person` `the day the copies were sent or delivered` `the day my employer's return is required to be filed with the Minister`

@export May my employer give me my portion in an electronic format (reg 13(3) and (4))?
GIVEN `my employer has my express consent in writing or in an electronic format` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given your employer your express consent in writing or in an electronic format?
      `my employer is precluded from providing it electronically under subsection 209(5) of the Income Tax Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer precluded from providing it electronically under subsection 209(5) of the Income Tax Regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my employer give me my portion in an electronic format` IF
    `reg 13(3) and (4) — the person may supply the employee's portion in an electronic format` `my employer has my express consent in writing or in an electronic format` `my employer is precluded from providing it electronically under subsection 209(5) of the Income Tax Regulations`

@export What penalty can my employer be made to pay for each day it fails to file a return as and when required (reg 14(1))?
GIVEN `my employer fails to file a return as and when required by this Part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer fail to file a return as and when this Part requires?
      `the number of days of default` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days has the default lasted?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What penalty can my employer be made to pay for failing to file a return as and when required` IS
    `reg 14(1) — the penalty for failing to file a return as and when required` `my employer fails to file a return as and when required by this Part` `the number of days of default`

@export What penalty can my employer be made to pay for failing to give me my copies (reg 14(2))?
GIVEN `my employer fails to comply with section 13` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer fail to comply with section 13 (giving you copies of your portion)?
      `the number of days of default` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days has the default lasted?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What penalty can my employer be made to pay for failing to give me my copies` IS
    `reg 14(2) — the penalty for failing to comply with section 13` `my employer fails to comply with section 13` `the number of days of default`

@export How many days has the default lasted (reg 14)?
GIVEN `the day by which the act was due` IS A DATE @desc By what day was the act due?
      `the day the act was done` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it done? (Today, if it has not been.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days has the default lasted` IS
    `reg 14 — the number of days of default` `the day by which the act was due` `the day the act was done`


§§ `D. Is my employment pensionable? One question for each route in and out (regs 15 to 34.1)`

-- Each question is one route the Regulations give for bringing employment into, or taking it out of, pensionable employment. A
-- route that the person's facts do not meet does not mean the employment is not pensionable by another route: ask the other routes too.
@export Is my employer an employer operating in Canada (reg 15(1))?
GIVEN `the kind of employer I work for` IS A `cr1 Kind of employer for the definition of employer operating in Canada` @desc Is your employer Her Majesty in right of Canada, Her Majesty in right of a province, an agent of Her Majesty in right of a province, or another kind of employer?
      `my employer's employment has been included in pensionable employment by regulation under paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has employment by that employer been included in pensionable employment by regulation in accordance with paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act?
      `my employer has an establishment in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer have an establishment in Canada?
      `my employer is subject to income tax under Part I of the Income Tax Act, or but for section 149 would be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer subject to income tax under Part I of the Income Tax Act, or would it be but for section 149 of that Act?
      `my employer has taxable income for the taxation year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer have taxable income for the taxation year?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employer an employer operating in Canada` IS
    `reg 15(1) — an employer is an employer operating in Canada` `the kind of employer I work for` `my employer's employment has been included in pensionable employment by regulation under paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act` `my employer has an establishment in Canada` `my employer is subject to income tax under Part I of the Income Tax Act, or but for section 149 would be` `my employer has taxable income for the taxation year`

@export Is my employment employment in international transportation (reg 15(1))?
GIVEN `the conveyance I work on` IS A `cr1 Conveyance in the definition of employment in international transportation` @desc On what do you work (a ship, an aircraft of a licensed international commercial air service, a freight or passenger train, a Canada-United States registered motor vehicle, or another conveyance)?
      `I am primarily engaged in this employment in a pay period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you primarily engaged in this employment in a pay period?
      `this employment is performed partly within and partly outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this employment performed partly within and partly outside Canada?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employment employment in international transportation` IF
    `reg 15(1) — employment is employment in international transportation` `the conveyance I work on` `I am primarily engaged in this employment in a pay period` `this employment is performed partly within and partly outside Canada`

@export Is this place an establishment in Canada of my employer (reg 15(1))?
GIVEN `the place or premises is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place or premises in Canada?
      `the place or premises is owned, leased or licensed by my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it owned, leased or licensed by your employer?
      `my employer or its employees work or report for work there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your employer or one or more of its employees work or report for work there?
      `one or more of my employer's employees are paid from or at it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are one or more of your employer's employees paid from or at it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this place an establishment in Canada of my employer` IF
    `reg 15(1) — a place is an establishment in Canada of an employer` `the place or premises is in Canada` `the place or premises is owned, leased or licensed by my employer` `my employer or its employees work or report for work there` `one or more of my employer's employees are paid from or at it`

@export Is this craft a ship (reg 15(1))?
GIVEN `it is a vessel, boat or craft` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a vessel, boat or craft?
      `it is used or designed to be used in navigation in, on, through or immediately above water` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it used or designed to be used in navigation in, on, through or immediately above water?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this craft a ship` IF
    `reg 15(1) — a craft is a ship` `it is a vessel, boat or craft` `it is used or designed to be used in navigation in, on, through or immediately above water`

-- Reg 16(1). The spouse's or partner's facts matter only to paragraph (e); the fields of their record that paragraphs (c), (d) and
-- 250(1)(b) never read are given FALSE here (placeholders), and so are the ones paragraph (e) reads of the employee, not the partner.
@export Is my employment outside Canada pensionable employment (reg 16(1))?
GIVEN `the employment is outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment outside Canada?
      `the employment is employment in international transportation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it employment in international transportation?
      `the employment would be pensionable employment if it were in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would it be pensionable employment if it were in Canada?
      `I ordinarily report for work at an establishment in Canada of my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you ordinarily report for work at an establishment in Canada of your employer?
      `I am resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you resident in Canada?
      `I am paid at or from an establishment in Canada of my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paid at or from an establishment in Canada of your employer?
      `I am employed by Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed by Her Majesty in right of Canada?
      `I am employed by Her Majesty in right of a province whose employment has been included by regulation under paragraph 7(1)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed by Her Majesty in right of a province whose employment has been included in pensionable employment by regulation in accordance with paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act?
      `I am employed by Her Majesty in right of a province whose government has entered into an agreement under paragraph 7(1)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed by Her Majesty in right of a province the government of which has entered into an agreement referred to in paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act?
      `I was engaged outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you engaged outside Canada?
      `I was engaged for the performance of services outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you engaged for the performance of services outside Canada?
      `I was resident in Canada immediately before becoming employed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you resident in Canada immediately before becoming employed outside Canada?
      `I receive a representation allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive a representation allowance?
      `I perform services in another country under a prescribed international development assistance program of the Government of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you perform services in a country other than Canada under an international development assistance program of the Government of Canada prescribed as such under paragraph 250(1)(d) of the Income Tax Act?
      `I was resident in Canada at any time in the three months before those services began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you resident in Canada at any time in the three-month period before the day those services began?
      `I am a person described in paragraph 250(1)(b) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person described in paragraph 250(1)(b) of the Income Tax Act?
      `I am living with my spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you living with your spouse or common-law partner?
      `I was resident in Canada at any time before becoming employed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you resident in Canada at any time before becoming employed outside Canada?
      `the President of the Treasury Board has signified to the Minister a wish that my employment be included` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the President of the Treasury Board signified to the Minister a wish that your employment be included in pensionable employment?
      `the government of my province has signified to the Minister a wish that my employment be included` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the government of your province signified to the Minister a wish that your employment be included in pensionable employment?
      `I have a spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a spouse or common-law partner whose employment outside Canada may matter?
      `my spouse or common-law partner: is employed by Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your spouse or common-law partner meet this description (asked of them): Are you employed by Her Majesty in right of Canada?
      `my spouse or common-law partner: is employed by Her Majesty in right of a province whose employment has been included by regulation under paragraph 7(1)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your spouse or common-law partner meet this description (asked of them): Are you employed by Her Majesty in right of a province whose employment has been included in pensionable employment by regulation in accordance with paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act?
      `my spouse or common-law partner: was engaged outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your spouse or common-law partner meet this description (asked of them): Were you engaged outside Canada?
      `my spouse or common-law partner: was engaged for the performance of services outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your spouse or common-law partner meet this description (asked of them): Were you engaged for the performance of services outside Canada?
      `my spouse or common-law partner: was resident in Canada immediately before becoming employed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your spouse or common-law partner meet this description (asked of them): Were you resident in Canada immediately before becoming employed outside Canada?
      `my spouse or common-law partner: receives a representation allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your spouse or common-law partner meet this description (asked of them): Do you receive a representation allowance?
      `my spouse or common-law partner: performs services in another country under a prescribed international development assistance program of the Government of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your spouse or common-law partner meet this description (asked of them): Do you perform services in a country other than Canada under an international development assistance program of the Government of Canada prescribed as such under paragraph 250(1)(d) of the Income Tax Act?
      `my spouse or common-law partner: was resident in Canada at any time in the three months before those services began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your spouse or common-law partner meet this description (asked of them): Were you resident in Canada at any time in the three-month period before the day those services began?
      `my spouse or common-law partner: is a person described in paragraph 250(1)(b) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your spouse or common-law partner meet this description (asked of them): Are you a person described in paragraph 250(1)(b) of the Income Tax Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employment outside Canada pensionable employment` IF
    `reg 16(1) — pensionable employment includes the employment outside Canada` `the employment is outside Canada` `the employment is employment in international transportation` `the employment would be pensionable employment if it were in Canada` me `my partner if I have one`
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS `cr1 Employee employed outside Canada` WITH
            `ordinarily reports for work at an establishment in Canada of the employer` IS `I ordinarily report for work at an establishment in Canada of my employer`
            `resident in Canada` IS `I am resident in Canada`
            `paid at or from an establishment in Canada of the employer` IS `I am paid at or from an establishment in Canada of my employer`
            `employed by Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS `I am employed by Her Majesty in right of Canada`
            `employed by Her Majesty in right of a province whose employment has been included in pensionable employment by regulation in accordance with paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act` IS `I am employed by Her Majesty in right of a province whose employment has been included by regulation under paragraph 7(1)(e)`
            `employed by Her Majesty in right of a province the government of which has entered into an agreement referred to in paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act` IS `I am employed by Her Majesty in right of a province whose government has entered into an agreement under paragraph 7(1)(e)`
            `engaged outside Canada` IS `I was engaged outside Canada`
            `engaged for the performance of services outside Canada` IS `I was engaged for the performance of services outside Canada`
            `resident in Canada immediately prior to becoming so employed outside Canada` IS `I was resident in Canada immediately before becoming employed outside Canada`
            `in receipt of a representation allowance` IS `I receive a representation allowance`
            `performs services in a country other than Canada under an international development assistance program of the Government of Canada prescribed as such pursuant to paragraph 250(1)(d) of the Income Tax Act` IS `I perform services in another country under a prescribed international development assistance program of the Government of Canada`
            `resident in Canada at any time in the three-month period preceding the day on which such services commenced` IS `I was resident in Canada at any time in the three months before those services began`
            `a person described in paragraph 250(1)(b) of the Income Tax Act` IS `I am a person described in paragraph 250(1)(b) of the Income Tax Act`
            `living with the spouse or common-law partner` IS `I am living with my spouse or common-law partner`
            `resident in Canada at any time before becoming so employed outside Canada` IS `I was resident in Canada at any time before becoming employed outside Canada`
            `the President of the Treasury Board signifies to the Minister that he wishes the employment of such employee to be included in pensionable employment` IS `the President of the Treasury Board has signified to the Minister a wish that my employment be included`
            `the government of the province signifies to the Minister that it wishes the employment of such employee to be included in pensionable employment` IS `the government of my province has signified to the Minister a wish that my employment be included`
        `my partner` MEANS `cr1 Employee employed outside Canada` WITH
            `ordinarily reports for work at an establishment in Canada of the employer` IS FALSE
            `resident in Canada` IS FALSE
            `paid at or from an establishment in Canada of the employer` IS FALSE
            `employed by Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS `my spouse or common-law partner: is employed by Her Majesty in right of Canada`
            `employed by Her Majesty in right of a province whose employment has been included in pensionable employment by regulation in accordance with paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act` IS `my spouse or common-law partner: is employed by Her Majesty in right of a province whose employment has been included by regulation under paragraph 7(1)(e)`
            `employed by Her Majesty in right of a province the government of which has entered into an agreement referred to in paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act` IS FALSE
            `engaged outside Canada` IS `my spouse or common-law partner: was engaged outside Canada`
            `engaged for the performance of services outside Canada` IS `my spouse or common-law partner: was engaged for the performance of services outside Canada`
            `resident in Canada immediately prior to becoming so employed outside Canada` IS `my spouse or common-law partner: was resident in Canada immediately before becoming employed outside Canada`
            `in receipt of a representation allowance` IS `my spouse or common-law partner: receives a representation allowance`
            `performs services in a country other than Canada under an international development assistance program of the Government of Canada prescribed as such pursuant to paragraph 250(1)(d) of the Income Tax Act` IS `my spouse or common-law partner: performs services in another country under a prescribed international development assistance program of the Government of Canada`
            `resident in Canada at any time in the three-month period preceding the day on which such services commenced` IS `my spouse or common-law partner: was resident in Canada at any time in the three months before those services began`
            `a person described in paragraph 250(1)(b) of the Income Tax Act` IS `my spouse or common-law partner: is a person described in paragraph 250(1)(b) of the Income Tax Act`
            `living with the spouse or common-law partner` IS FALSE
            `resident in Canada at any time before becoming so employed outside Canada` IS FALSE
            `the President of the Treasury Board signifies to the Minister that he wishes the employment of such employee to be included in pensionable employment` IS FALSE
            `the government of the province signifies to the Minister that it wishes the employment of such employee to be included in pensionable employment` IS FALSE
        `my partner if I have one` MEANS IF `I have a spouse or common-law partner` THEN JUST `my partner` ELSE NOTHING

@export Is my employment in another country pensionable employment because my Canadian employer has undertaken to pay the contributions (reg 16(2))?
GIVEN `my employment is in a country other than Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment in a country other than Canada?
      `my employment is described in subsection 16(1) or is employment in international transportation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment described in subsection 16(1) or is it employment in international transportation?
      `my employer is an employer operating in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer an employer operating in Canada?
      `my employment would be pensionable employment if it were in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your employment be pensionable employment if it were in Canada?
      `I was engaged by my employer when I was in and resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you engaged by your employer when you were in and resident in Canada?
      `I ceased to be employed outside Canada as a member of the Canadian Forces or in the circumstances described in 16(1)(c), (d) or (e)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cease to be employed outside Canada as a member of the Canadian Forces or in the circumstances described in 16(1)(c), (d) or (e)?
      `the day I ceased to be so employed` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you cease to be so employed? (Any date if you did not.)
      `the day my employer engaged me` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your employer engage you?
      `my employer has undertaken to make payment of the contributions in accordance with section 8 in respect of all such employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employer undertaken to make payment of the contributions in accordance with section 8 in respect of all such employees?
      `the undertaking is in a form the Minister has authorized` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the undertaking in a form the Minister has authorized?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employment in another country pensionable employment because my Canadian employer has undertaken to pay the contributions` IF
    `reg 16(2) — pensionable employment includes the employment in another country` `my employment is in a country other than Canada` `my employment is described in subsection 16(1) or is employment in international transportation` `my employer is an employer operating in Canada` `my employment would be pensionable employment if it were in Canada` `I was engaged by my employer when I was in and resident in Canada` (`cr1 seat: a day if it has happened` `I ceased to be employed outside Canada as a member of the Canadian Forces or in the circumstances described in 16(1)(c), (d) or (e)` `the day I ceased to be so employed`) `the day my employer engaged me` `my employer has undertaken to make payment of the contributions in accordance with section 8 in respect of all such employees` `the undertaking is in a form the Minister has authorized`

@export Is my employment in international transportation pensionable (reg 17(1))?
GIVEN `my employment is described in section 18, 19, 20 or 21` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment described in regulation 18, 19, 20 or 21?
      `my employment would be pensionable employment if it were wholly within Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your employment be pensionable employment if it were wholly within Canada?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employment in international transportation pensionable` IF
    `reg 17(1) — employment in international transportation described in sections 18 to 21 is pensionable employment` `my employment is described in section 18, 19, 20 or 21` `my employment would be pensionable employment if it were wholly within Canada`

@export Is my employment in international transportation excepted from pensionable employment (reg 17(2))?
GIVEN `my employment is included in pensionable employment by section 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment included in pensionable employment by regulation 18?
      `my employment is included in pensionable employment by section 19` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it included by regulation 19?
      `my employment is included in pensionable employment by section 20` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it included by regulation 20?
      `my employment is included in pensionable employment by section 21` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it included by regulation 21?
      `my employment is included in pensionable employment by section 22` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it included by regulation 22?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employment in international transportation excepted from pensionable employment` IF
    `reg 17(2) — employment in international transportation is excepted from pensionable employment` `my employment is included in pensionable employment by section 18` `my employment is included in pensionable employment by section 19` `my employment is included in pensionable employment by section 20` `my employment is included in pensionable employment by section 21` `my employment is included in pensionable employment by section 22`

@export Is my employment on a ship under an agreement with the crew pensionable (reg 18(1))?
GIVEN `my employer is an employer operating in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer an employer operating in Canada?
      `the ship is operated under an agreement with the crew that is entered into in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ship operated under an agreement with the crew that is entered into in Canada?
      `the ship is engaged on an inland voyage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ship engaged on an inland voyage?
      `I have a place of domicile in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a place of domicile in Canada?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employment on a ship under an agreement with the crew pensionable` IF
    `reg 18(1) — pensionable employment includes the employment on the ship under an agreement with the crew` `my employer is an employer operating in Canada` `the ship is operated under an agreement with the crew that is entered into in Canada` `the ship is engaged on an inland voyage` `I have a place of domicile in Canada`

@export Is my employment on a ship not under an agreement with the crew pensionable (reg 18(2))?
GIVEN `my employer is an employer operating in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer an employer operating in Canada?
      `the ship is operating under an agreement with the crew` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ship operating under an agreement with the crew?
      `the ship is being operated mainly in and near Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ship being operated mainly in and near Canada?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employment on a ship not under an agreement with the crew pensionable` IF
    `reg 18(2) — pensionable employment includes the employment on the ship not under an agreement with the crew` `my employer is an employer operating in Canada` `the ship is operating under an agreement with the crew` `the ship is being operated mainly in and near Canada`

@export Do I have a place of domicile in Canada (reg 18(3))?
GIVEN `I am a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a Canadian citizen?
      `I am a permanent resident within the meaning of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a permanent resident within the meaning of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act?
      `I have a place in Canada to which I return from time to time as my place of permanent abode` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a place in Canada to which you return from time to time as your place of permanent abode?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have a place of domicile in Canada` IF
    `reg 18(3) — a person has a place of domicile in Canada` `I am a Canadian citizen` `I am a permanent resident within the meaning of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act` `I have a place in Canada to which I return from time to time as my place of permanent abode`

@export Is my agreement with the crew an agreement with the crew for this regulation (reg 18(4))?
GIVEN `the agreement is articles of agreement entered into under the Canada Shipping Act, 2001` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement articles of agreement entered into under the Canada Shipping Act, 2001?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my agreement with the crew an agreement with the crew for this regulation` IF
    `reg 18(4) — an agreement is an agreement with the crew` `the agreement is articles of agreement entered into under the Canada Shipping Act, 2001`

@export Is my ship's voyage an inland voyage (reg 18(4))?
GIVEN `the waters of the voyage` IS A `cr1 Waters on which a voyage is made` @desc On what waters is the voyage made (navigable fresh waters within Canada, inland waters within the United States, Lake Michigan, sheltered coastal waters described in Schedule 1 to the Vessel Safety Certificates Regulations, or other waters)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my ship's voyage an inland voyage` IF
    `reg 18(4) — a voyage is an inland voyage` `the waters of the voyage`

@export Is my employment on an aircraft pensionable (reg 19)?
GIVEN `my employment is in international transportation on an aircraft used in the operation of a commercial air service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment in international transportation on an aircraft used in the operation of a commercial air service?
      `the person who operates the service is licensed to operate an international service under the Canada Transportation Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who operates the service licensed to operate an international service under the Canada Transportation Act?
      `the person who operates the service is licensed to operate a domestic service under the Canada Transportation Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person also licensed to operate a domestic service under the Canada Transportation Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employment on an aircraft pensionable` IF
    `reg 19 — pensionable employment includes the employment on the aircraft` `my employment is in international transportation on an aircraft used in the operation of a commercial air service` `the person who operates the service is licensed to operate an international service under the Canada Transportation Act` `the person who operates the service is licensed to operate a domestic service under the Canada Transportation Act`

@export How much of my employment on a train of a Canadian railway company is pensionable (reg 20(1))?
GIVEN `my employment is in international transportation on a freight or passenger train` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment in international transportation on a freight or passenger train?
      `the train is operated by a railway company whose principal place of business is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the train operated by a railway company, within the meaning of the Canada Transportation Act, whose principal place of business is in Canada?
      `the part of my employment my employer determined to be employment in Canada` IS A NUMBER @desc What part of your employment did your employer determine to be employment in Canada (as a fraction, or the number your employer states)?
      `the Minister has approved the basis on which my employer determined it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister approved the basis on which your employer determined it?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my employment on a train of a Canadian railway company is pensionable` IS
    `reg 20(1) — the part of the employment on a train of a Canadian railway company that is pensionable employment` `my employment is in international transportation on a freight or passenger train` `the train is operated by a railway company whose principal place of business is in Canada` `the part of my employment my employer determined to be employment in Canada` `the Minister has approved the basis on which my employer determined it`

@export How much of my employment on a train of a foreign railway company is pensionable (reg 20(2))?
GIVEN `my employment is in international transportation on a freight or passenger train` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment in international transportation on a freight or passenger train?
      `the train is operated by a railway company whose principal place of business is outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the train operated by a railway company, within the meaning of the Canada Transportation Act, whose principal place of business is outside Canada?
      `I am resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you resident in Canada?
      `the part of my employment my employer determined to be employment in Canada` IS A NUMBER @desc What part of your employment did your employer determine to be employment in Canada (as a fraction, or the number your employer states)?
      `the Minister has approved the basis on which my employer determined it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister approved the basis on which your employer determined it?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my employment on a train of a foreign railway company is pensionable` IS
    `reg 20(2) — the part of the employment on a train of a foreign railway company that is pensionable employment` `my employment is in international transportation on a freight or passenger train` `the train is operated by a railway company whose principal place of business is outside Canada` `I am resident in Canada` `the part of my employment my employer determined to be employment in Canada` `the Minister has approved the basis on which my employer determined it`

@export Is my employment on a motor vehicle pensionable (reg 21)?
GIVEN `my employment is in international transportation on a motor vehicle registered to operate in one or more provinces and in one or more states of the United States` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment in international transportation on a motor vehicle registered to operate in one or more provinces of Canada and in one or more states of the United States?
      `I am resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you resident in Canada?
      `the motor vehicle is operated for an enterprise regarded for tax as an enterprise of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the motor vehicle operated for the purposes of an enterprise regarded for the purpose of taxation under the Income Tax Act as an enterprise of Canada?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employment on a motor vehicle pensionable` IF
    `reg 21 — pensionable employment includes the employment on the motor vehicle` `my employment is in international transportation on a motor vehicle registered to operate in one or more provinces and in one or more states of the United States` `I am resident in Canada` `the motor vehicle is operated for an enterprise regarded for tax as an enterprise of Canada`

@export Is all of my employment excepted because my employer is not resident in Canada and has no establishment here (reg 22(1))?
GIVEN `my employer is resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer resident in Canada?
      `my employer has an establishment in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer have an establishment in Canada?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is all of my employment excepted because my employer is not resident in Canada and has no establishment here` IF
    `reg 22(1) — the entire employment by an employer not resident in Canada and without an establishment in Canada is excepted` `my employer is resident in Canada` `my employer has an establishment in Canada`

@export Is my employment in Canada, under an employer not resident here, pensionable (reg 22(2)(a))?
GIVEN `my employment is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment in Canada?
      `I am resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you resident in Canada?
      `my employer is resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer resident in Canada?
      `my employer has an establishment in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer have an establishment in Canada?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employment in Canada under an employer not resident here pensionable under paragraph (2)(a)` IF
    `reg 22(2)(a) — the employment in Canada of a person resident in Canada by an employer not resident and without an establishment` `my employment is in Canada` `I am resident in Canada` `my employer is resident in Canada` `my employer has an establishment in Canada`

@export Is the part in Canada of my employment on a United States enterprise's motor vehicle pensionable (reg 22(2)(b))?
GIVEN `I am resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you resident in Canada?
      `I am employed in international transportation on a motor vehicle registered to operate in Canada and the United States` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in international transportation on a motor vehicle registered to operate in one or more provinces of Canada and in one or more states of the United States?
      `the motor vehicle is operated for an enterprise regarded for tax as an enterprise of the United States` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the motor vehicle operated for the purposes of an enterprise regarded for the purpose of taxation under the Income Tax Act as an enterprise of the United States?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the part in Canada of my employment on a United States enterprise's motor vehicle pensionable` IF
    `reg 22(2)(b) — the part in Canada of the employment of a person resident in Canada on a motor vehicle of an enterprise of the United States` `I am resident in Canada` `I am employed in international transportation on a motor vehicle registered to operate in Canada and the United States` `the motor vehicle is operated for an enterprise regarded for tax as an enterprise of the United States`

@export Is my employment under an employer not resident in Canada pensionable because arrangements have been made (reg 22(2) and (3))?
GIVEN `my employment is described in paragraph 22(2)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment described in regulation 22(2)(a) or (b)?
      `the name of my province` IS A STRING @desc What is the name of the province where you work?
      `my province provides a comprehensive pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that province provide a comprehensive pension plan?
      `my employer has made arrangements satisfactory to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employer made arrangements satisfactory to the Minister? (The Minister must be satisfied that they secure payment of the contributions under section 8 and the filing of the returns required by Part II.)
      `my employer has made arrangements satisfactory to the authority administering the provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employer made arrangements satisfactory to the authority having the administration of the provincial pension plan for the payment of contributions under that plan?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employment under an employer not resident in Canada pensionable because arrangements have been made` IF
    `reg 22(2) and (3) — pensionable employment includes the employment of a person under an employer not resident in Canada` `my employment is described in paragraph 22(2)(a) or (b)` `my province` `my employer has made arrangements satisfactory to the Minister` `my employer has made arrangements satisfactory to the authority administering the provincial pension plan`
    WHERE
        `my province` MEANS Province WITH
            `name of the province` IS `the name of my province`
            `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS `my province provides a comprehensive pension plan`

@export What does regulation 22 do to my employment (reg 22)?
GIVEN `my employment is included by subsection 22(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment included in pensionable employment by regulation 22(2)?
      `my employment is excepted by subsection 22(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment excepted by regulation 22(1)?
GIVETH A `cr1 Effect of regulation 22 on an employment`
DECIDE `What does regulation 22 do to my employment` IS
    `reg 22 — the effect of regulation 22 on the employment` `my employment is included by subsection 22(2)` `my employment is excepted by subsection 22(1)`

@export Does paragraph 15(1)(b) of the Act not apply to my employment (reg 22(4))?
GIVEN `my employment is included in pensionable employment by subsection 22(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment included in pensionable employment by regulation 22(2)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does paragraph 15(1)(b) of the Act not apply to my employment under regulation 22` IF
    `reg 22(4) — paragraph 15(1)(b) of the Act does not apply to the employment` `my employment is included in pensionable employment by subsection 22(2)`

@export In which province am I deemed to report for work (reg 22(5))?
GIVEN `I am an employee referred to in subsection 22(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an employee referred to in regulation 22(2)?
      `my employer has an establishment in Canada within the meaning of subsection 4(4) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer have an establishment in Canada within the meaning of subsection 4(4) of the Act?
      `I ordinarily work or do the most work in a province of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you ordinarily work, or ordinarily do the most work, in a province of Canada?
      `the name of the province where I ordinarily work or do the most work` IS A STRING @desc What is the name of that province? (Anything if you do not work in one.)
      `that province provides a comprehensive pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that province provide a comprehensive pension plan?
      `the name of the province where I live` IS A STRING @desc What is the name of the province where you live?
      `the province where I live provides a comprehensive pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the province where you live provide a comprehensive pension plan?
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `In which province am I deemed to report for work` IS
    CONSIDER (`reg 22(5) — the province in which the employee is deemed to report for work` `I am an employee referred to in subsection 22(2)` `my employer has an establishment in Canada within the meaning of subsection 4(4) of the Act` `the province where I work if I work in one` `the province where I live`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST chosen THEN JUST (chosen's `name of the province`)
    WHERE
        `the province where I work` MEANS Province WITH
            `name of the province` IS `the name of the province where I ordinarily work or do the most work`
            `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS `that province provides a comprehensive pension plan`
        `the province where I live` MEANS Province WITH
            `name of the province` IS `the name of the province where I live`
            `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS `the province where I live provides a comprehensive pension plan`
        `the province where I work if I work in one` MEANS IF `I ordinarily work or do the most work in a province of Canada` THEN JUST `the province where I work` ELSE NOTHING

@export Is my employment as a director excepted because I am not ordinarily resident in Canada (reg 23)?
GIVEN `I am ordinarily resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ordinarily resident in Canada?
      `I am employed under a contract of service or apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed under a contract of service or apprenticeship?
      `I hold the tenure of an office other than a directorship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the tenure of an office other than a directorship?
      `I hold the position of a corporation director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the position of a corporation director?
      `my employment as such director is performed wholly or partly outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment as such a director performed wholly or partly outside Canada?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employment as a director excepted because I am not ordinarily resident in Canada` IF
    `reg 23 — the employment of a director not ordinarily resident in Canada is excepted` `I am ordinarily resident in Canada` `I am employed under a contract of service or apprenticeship` `I hold the tenure of an office other than a directorship` `I hold the position of a corporation director` `my employment as such director is performed wholly or partly outside Canada`

@export Is my employment by a province, or by its agent, included in pensionable employment by regulation 24(1)?
GIVEN `the heading of my province in Schedule III` IS A STRING @desc Which province is named in Schedule III as your employer's province? (Write its name as the Schedule does.)
      `my employment is by Her Majesty in right of that province or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of that province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment by Her Majesty in right of that province, or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of that province?
      `my employment is set out in Schedule IV` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment set out in Schedule IV?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employment by a province or by its agent included in pensionable employment by regulation 24(1)` IF
    `reg 24(1) — employment by a province named in Schedule III or its agent is included` `the heading of my province in Schedule III` `my employment is by Her Majesty in right of that province or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of that province` `my employment is set out in Schedule IV`

@export Is my employment set out in Schedule IV (reg 24, Schedule IV)?
GIVEN `the heading in Schedule IV that names my employment` IS A STRING @desc Under which heading of Schedule IV does your employment fall?
      `the lettered paragraph in Schedule IV that names my employment` IS A STRING @desc Which lettered paragraph under that heading? (Leave it empty if there is none.)
      `my employment meets the words of that paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employment meet the words of that paragraph?
      `my duties require my full time attention and I receive a regular salary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your duties require your full time attention, and do you receive a regular salary for them?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employment set out in Schedule IV` IF
    `Schedule IV — the employment is set out` `the heading in Schedule IV that names my employment` `the lettered paragraph in Schedule IV that names my employment` `my employment meets the words of that paragraph` `my duties require my full time attention and I receive a regular salary`

@export Is my employment by a province with a comprehensive pension plan, or its agent, included (reg 24(2))?
GIVEN `the name of the province` IS A STRING @desc What is the name of the province?
      `the province provides a comprehensive pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the province provide a comprehensive pension plan?
      `my employment is by Her Majesty in right of that province or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of that province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment by Her Majesty in right of that province, or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of that province?
      `my employment is pensionable employment under the provincial pension plan of that province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment pensionable employment under the provincial pension plan of that province?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employment by a province with a comprehensive pension plan or its agent included` IF
    `reg 24(2) — employment by a province providing a comprehensive pension plan or its agent is included` `the province` `my employment is by Her Majesty in right of that province or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of that province` `my employment is pensionable employment under the provincial pension plan of that province`
    WHERE
        `the province` MEANS Province WITH
            `name of the province` IS `the name of the province`
            `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS `the province provides a comprehensive pension plan`

@export Do the Act's contribution provisions and Part III of the Act not apply to my employment (reg 24(3))?
GIVEN `my employment is included in pensionable employment by virtue of subsection 24(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment included in pensionable employment by virtue of regulation 24(2)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the Act's contribution provisions and Part III of the Act not apply to my employment` IF
    `reg 24(3) — the Act's provisions on contributions and Part III of the Act do not apply to the employment` `my employment is included in pensionable employment by virtue of subsection 24(2)`

@export Is my employment in Canada by an international organization included in pensionable employment (reg 25)?
GIVEN `my employment is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment in Canada?
      `the name of the international organization` IS A STRING @desc What is the name of the international organization? (Write it as Schedule V does.)
      `I am exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of a Tax Convention to which Canada is a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of a Tax Convention to which Canada is a party?
      `I am exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(a) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(a) of the Income Tax Act?
      `I am exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of an order of the Governor in Council` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of an order of the Governor in Council?
      `I am a citizen within the meaning of section 3 of the Citizenship Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a citizen within the meaning of section 3 of the Citizenship Act?
      `I am a permanent resident as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Immigration Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a permanent resident as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Immigration Act?
      `I am an official of the Commonwealth of Learning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an official of the Commonwealth of Learning?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employment in Canada by an international organization included in pensionable employment` IF
    `reg 25 — employment in Canada by an international organization is included` `my employment is in Canada` `the name of the international organization` `me`
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS `cr1 Person employed by an international organization` WITH
            `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of a Tax Convention to which Canada is a party` IS `I am exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of a Tax Convention to which Canada is a party`
            `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(a) of the Income Tax Act` IS `I am exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(a) of the Income Tax Act`
            `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of an order of the Governor in Council` IS `I am exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of an order of the Governor in Council`
            `a citizen within the meaning of section 3 of the Citizenship Act` IS `I am a citizen within the meaning of section 3 of the Citizenship Act`
            `a permanent resident as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Immigration Act` IS `I am a permanent resident as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Immigration Act`
            `an official of the Commonwealth of Learning` IS `I am an official of the Commonwealth of Learning`

@export Is my employment in Canada by the government of another country included in pensionable employment (reg 26)?
GIVEN `my employment is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment in Canada?
      `the name of the country whose government employs me` IS A STRING @desc What is the name of the country whose government employs you? (Write it as Schedule VII does.)
      `I am a subject or citizen of New Zealand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a subject or citizen of New Zealand?
      `I am exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of the New Zealand-Canada Tax Convention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of the New Zealand-Canada Tax Convention?
      `I am a citizen of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a citizen of Canada?
      `I am permanently resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you permanently resident in Canada?
      `I contribute to a pension plan of the French Republic, or the French Republic contributes on my behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you contribute to a pension plan of the French Republic, or does the French Republic make contributions on your behalf to such a plan?
      `I am exempt from Canadian income tax` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you exempt from Canadian income tax?
      `I am a citizen of the United States` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a citizen of the United States?
      `I participate in the Civil Service Retirement System of the United States or another plan financed by that government, have done so continuously since before October 1, 1983 and have elected not to participate in the Canada Pension Plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you participate in the Civil Service Retirement System of the United States or another pension plan financed by the Government of the United States, have you done so continuously since before October 1, 1983, and have you elected not to participate in the Canada Pension Plan?
      `I am a locally engaged employee of the Government of the United States` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a locally engaged employee of the Government of the United States?
      `I am a national of Japan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a national of Japan?
      `I am a national of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a national of Canada?
      `I am exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of the Canada-Japan Income Tax Convention Act, 1965` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of the Canada-Japan Income Tax Convention Act, 1965?
      `I am exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(a) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(a) of the Income Tax Act?
      `I am exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(b) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(b) of the Income Tax Act?
      `I participate in the Government of Malaysia's non-contributory gratuity scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you participate in the Government of Malaysia's non-contributory gratuity scheme?
      `I am a citizen of Senegal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a citizen of Senegal?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employment in Canada by the government of another country included in pensionable employment` IF
    `reg 26 — employment in Canada by the government of a country other than Canada is included` `my employment is in Canada` `the name of the country whose government employs me` `me`
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS `cr1 Person employed by a foreign government` WITH
            `a subject or citizen of New Zealand` IS `I am a subject or citizen of New Zealand`
            `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of the New Zealand-Canada Tax Convention` IS `I am exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of the New Zealand-Canada Tax Convention`
            `a citizen of Canada` IS `I am a citizen of Canada`
            `permanently resident in Canada` IS `I am permanently resident in Canada`
            `contributes to a pension plan of the French Republic, or has contributions made on their behalf to such a plan by the French Republic` IS `I contribute to a pension plan of the French Republic, or the French Republic contributes on my behalf`
            `exempt from Canadian income tax` IS `I am exempt from Canadian income tax`
            `a citizen of the United States` IS `I am a citizen of the United States`
            `participates in the Civil Service Retirement System of the United States or another pension plan financed by the Government of the United States, has done so continuously since before October 1, 1983 and has elected not to participate in the Canada Pension Plan` IS `I participate in the Civil Service Retirement System of the United States or another plan financed by that government, have done so continuously since before October 1, 1983 and have elected not to participate in the Canada Pension Plan`
            `a locally engaged employee of the Government of the United States` IS `I am a locally engaged employee of the Government of the United States`
            `a national of Japan` IS `I am a national of Japan`
            `a national of Canada` IS `I am a national of Canada`
            `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of the Canada-Japan Income Tax Convention Act, 1965` IS `I am exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of the Canada-Japan Income Tax Convention Act, 1965`
            `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(a) of the Income Tax Act` IS `I am exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(a) of the Income Tax Act`
            `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(b) of the Income Tax Act` IS `I am exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(b) of the Income Tax Act`
            `participates in the Government of Malaysia's non-contributory gratuity scheme` IS `I participate in the Government of Malaysia's non-contributory gratuity scheme`
            `a citizen of Senegal` IS `I am a citizen of Senegal`

@export Is my employment as a member of a religious order included in pensionable employment (reg 27)?
GIVEN `my employment is referred to in paragraph 6(2)(e) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment, as a member of a religious order who has taken a vow of perpetual poverty, referred to in paragraph 6(2)(e) of the Act?
