§§ `E. Interest on a refund of my overpayment (regs 35 and 36)`

-- Regulation 36(2) fixes the rate from Treasury Bill yields that someone else publishes. The seat asks for the one published figure
-- the rule takes the mean of: the average equivalent yield of three-month Treasury Bills sold at auction in the first month of
-- the quarter before the quarter in question, as a percentage. The rule rounds it up to a whole percentage itself.
@export From what day does interest run on my refund of an overpayment (reg 35(a))?
GIVEN `the year for which I paid the contributions` IS A NUMBER @desc For which calendar year did you pay the contributions?
      `an application for the refund was received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you apply for the refund?
      `the day my application for the refund was received` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your application received? (Any date if you did not apply.)
      `the day the overpayment arose` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the overpayment arise?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From what day does interest run on my refund of an overpayment` IS
    `reg 35(a) — the first day of the period for which interest runs on an overpayment refunded to an employee or a self-employed person` `the year for which I paid the contributions` (`cr1 seat: a day if it has happened` `an application for the refund was received` `the day my application for the refund was received`) `the day the overpayment arose`

@export From what day does interest run on my employer's refund of an overpayment (reg 35(b))?
GIVEN `the day the remittance that created the overpayment was received` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the remittance that created the overpayment received?
      `the day that remittance was due to be received` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it due to be received?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From what day does interest run on my employer's refund of an overpayment` IS
    `reg 35(b) — the first day of the period for which interest runs on an overpayment refunded to an employer` `the day the remittance that created the overpayment was received` `the day that remittance was due to be received`

@export At what rate is interest paid to me on an amount the Minister owes me (reg 36(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the mean of the Treasury Bill yields for the first month of the preceding quarter, as a percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the simple arithmetic mean, as a percentage per annum, of the average equivalent yields of three-month Government of Canada Treasury Bills sold at auction in the first month of the quarter before the quarter in question? (For example, 4.37 for 4.37 per cent.)
      `the amount payable to me is payable to a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount payable to a corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `At what rate is interest paid to me on an amount the Minister owes me` IS
    `reg 36(2)(b) — the prescribed rate on an amount payable by the Minister` (LIST `the mean of the Treasury Bill yields for the first month of the preceding quarter, as a percentage`) `the amount payable to me is payable to a corporation`

@export At what rate is interest charged to me on an amount I owe the Receiver General (reg 36(2)(a))?
GIVEN `the mean of the Treasury Bill yields for the first month of the preceding quarter, as a percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the simple arithmetic mean, as a percentage per annum, of the average equivalent yields of three-month Government of Canada Treasury Bills sold at auction in the first month of the quarter before the quarter in question? (For example, 4.37 for 4.37 per cent.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `At what rate is interest charged to me on an amount I owe the Receiver General` IS
    `reg 36(2)(a) — the prescribed rate on an amount payable to the Receiver General` (LIST `the mean of the Treasury Bill yields for the first month of the preceding quarter, as a percentage`)

@export Which quarter of the year is this day in (reg 36(1))?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc Which day?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Which quarter of the year is this day in` IS
    `reg 36(1) — the number of the quarter of a year that contains a day` `the day`

@export Which month's Treasury Bill auctions fix the rate for the quarter this day is in (reg 36(2)(a)(i))?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc Which day?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Which month's Treasury Bill auctions fix the rate for the quarter this day is in` IS
    `reg 36(2)(a)(i) — the first month of the quarter preceding the quarter that contains a day` `the day`


§§ `F. My elections and their deadlines, and international agreements (regs 79 to 86)`

-- Regulation 79 (the Minister's power to make agreements) and regulation 85 (when the Minister calculates the Year's Maximum
-- Pensionable Earnings, and how the figures are rounded) are for an official; no question is asked of the individual about them.
