    `reg 84 — the individual's contributory salary and wages for the year are included as self-employed earnings` `subsection 13(3) of the Act applies to me for the year` `the year for which I elect` `I filed the form with my income tax return, or with the Minister if my return had already been filed` `the form is one the Minister has authorized` `the day I filed the form`

@export How much of my income from self-employment on a reserve counts (reg 84.1)?
GIVEN `I am an Indian, as defined in the Indian Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an Indian, as defined in the Indian Act?
      `the amount described in paragraph 14(a) of the Act for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount described in paragraph 14(a) of the Act for the year, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my income from self-employment on a reserve counts` IS
    `reg 84.1 — the extent of the income of the Indian for the year from self-employment on a reserve` `I am an Indian, as defined in the Indian Act` `the amount described in paragraph 14(a) of the Act for the year`

@export Does an international agreement treat my common-law partner as a spouse (reg 86)?
GIVEN `the country whose agreement is in question` IS A STRING @desc Which country's agreement is in question? (Write the country as Schedule IX does.)
      `my partner is cohabiting with me in a conjugal relationship at the relevant time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner cohabiting with you in a conjugal relationship at the relevant time?
      `the day our continuous cohabitation began` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your continuous cohabitation begin?
      `the relevant time` IS A DATE @desc What is the relevant time (for example, the day of the contributor's death)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does an international agreement treat my common-law partner as a spouse` IF
    `reg 86 — the agreement is applied so that the person has the treatment afforded to a spouse` `the country whose agreement is in question` `my partner is cohabiting with me in a conjugal relationship at the relevant time` `the day our continuous cohabitation began` `the relevant time`


§§ `G. Interest on a debt I owe the Crown (reg 87)`

@export Is this amount I owe a debt for the purposes of interest (reg 87(1))?
GIVEN `the kind of amount I owe` IS A `cr1 Kind of amount owing for the definition of a debt` @desc What is the amount (a debt under subsection 66(2) of the Act on which a penalty was imposed under section 90.1, a debt under subsection 66(2.02) of the Act, or another amount)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this amount I owe a debt for the purposes of interest` IF
    `reg 87(1) — an amount owing is a debt` `the kind of amount I owe`

@export Is what I received a demand for payment (reg 87(1))?
GIVEN `it is a demand for payment in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a demand for payment in writing?
      `it is a notification of a decision to impose a penalty under section 90.1 of the Act, or of the amount of a penalty imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a notification of a decision to impose a penalty under section 90.1 of the Act, or of the amount of a penalty imposed under that section?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I received a demand for payment` IF
    `reg 87(1) — a communication is a demand for payment` `it is a demand for payment in writing` `it is a notification of a decision to impose a penalty under section 90.1 of the Act, or of the amount of a penalty imposed`

@export Is this day a due date on my debt (reg 87(1))?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc Which day?
      `a payment schedule has been established` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a payment schedule been established?
      `the day a scheduled payment is to be made` IS A DATE @desc On what day is a scheduled payment to be made? (Any date if there is no schedule.)
      `the day on which the demand for payment was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the demand for payment issued?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this day a due date on my debt` IF
    `reg 87(1) — a day is a due date of the debt` `the day` `a payment schedule has been established` (LIST `the day a scheduled payment is to be made`) `the day on which the demand for payment was issued`

@export Is interest payable on my debt (reg 87(2))?
GIVEN `my debt is recoverable on or after the day regulation 87 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your debt recoverable on or after the day regulation 87 comes into force?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is interest payable on my debt` IF
    `reg 87(2) — interest is payable on the debt` `my debt is recoverable on or after the day regulation 87 comes into force`

@export From what day does interest accrue on my debt (reg 87(3))?
GIVEN `the due date of my debt` IS A DATE @desc What is the due date of your debt?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From what day does interest accrue on my debt` IS
    `reg 87(3) — the day the accrual of interest on the debt begins` `the due date of my debt`

@export At what rate does interest accrue on my debt (reg 87(4))?
GIVEN `the average bank rate for the month before the month in question, as a fraction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the simple arithmetic mean of the Bank of Canada's weekly bank rates established during the month before the month in question, as a fraction (5 per cent is 0.05)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `At what rate does interest accrue on my debt` IS
    `reg 87(4) — the rate at which interest accrues on the debt` `the average bank rate for the month before the month in question, as a fraction`

@export How much interest accrues on my balance in one month (reg 87(4))?
GIVEN `my balance` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your balance, in dollars?
      `the rate at which interest accrues, as a fraction` IS A NUMBER @desc At what annual rate does interest accrue, as a fraction? (The previous question.)
      `the number of days in the month on which interest accrues` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many days in the month does interest accrue?
      `the number of days in the year on which the daily rate is based` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many days in the year is the daily rate based? (The text does not say; ask the Minister.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much interest accrues on my balance in one month` IS
    `reg 87(4) — the interest that accrues on a balance in one month` `my balance` `the rate at which interest accrues, as a fraction` `the number of days in the month on which interest accrues` `the number of days in the year on which the daily rate is based`

@export What is my balance after the month's interest is compounded (reg 87(4))?
GIVEN `my balance` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your balance, in dollars?
      `the rate at which interest accrues, as a fraction` IS A NUMBER @desc At what annual rate does interest accrue, as a fraction?
      `the number of days in the month on which interest accrues` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many days in the month does interest accrue?
      `the number of days in the year on which the daily rate is based` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many days in the year is the daily rate based?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my balance after the month's interest is compounded` IS
    `reg 87(4) — the balance after the month's interest is compounded` `my balance` `the rate at which interest accrues, as a fraction` `the number of days in the month on which interest accrues` `the number of days in the year on which the daily rate is based`

@export Does interest accrue on my debt on this day (reg 87(5))?
GIVEN `a reconsideration under subsection 81(2) of the Act is pending in respect of the debt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a reconsideration under subsection 81(2) of the Act pending in respect of the debt?
      `an appeal under section 82 of the Act or section 55 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act is pending` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an appeal under section 82 of the Act or section 55 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act pending in respect of the debt?
      `a judicial review under the Federal Courts Act is pending` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a judicial review under the Federal Courts Act pending in respect of the debt?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does interest accrue on my debt on this day` IF
    `reg 87(5) — interest accrues on the debt on the day` `a reconsideration under subsection 81(2) of the Act is pending in respect of the debt` `an appeal under section 82 of the Act or section 55 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act is pending` `a judicial review under the Federal Courts Act is pending`

@export On what day does interest stop accruing on my debt (reg 87(6))?
GIVEN `a scheduled payment, or a payment of the debt in full, has been received by Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a scheduled payment, or a payment of the debt in full, been received by Her Majesty?
      `the day it was received` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it received? (Any date if not.)
      `the debt or part of it has been remitted under subsection 66(3) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the debt or a portion of it been remitted under subsection 66(3) of the Act?
      `the day it was remitted` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it remitted? (Any date if not.)
      `the penalty was reduced or the decision imposing it rescinded under subsection 90.1(4) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the penalty reduced, or the decision imposing it rescinded, under subsection 90.1(4) of the Act?
      `the day it was reduced or rescinded` IS A DATE @desc On what day? (Any date if not.)
      `there is a decision on the penalty by the Minister under subsection 81(2), or on an appeal or judicial review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a decision of the Minister under subsection 81(2) of the Act, or on an appeal under section 82 of the Act or a judicial review under the Federal Courts Act, in respect of the penalty?
      `the day of the latest of those decisions` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the latest of those decisions? (Any date if none.)
      `the accrued interest has been remitted under subsection 87(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the accrued interest been remitted under regulation 87(7)?
      `the day the interest was remitted` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it remitted? (Any date if not.)
      `the debtor has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the debtor died?
      `the day the debtor died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the debtor die? (Any date if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day does interest stop accruing on my debt` IS
    `reg 87(6) — the day the accrual of interest on the debt ceases`
        (`cr1 seat: a day if it has happened` `a scheduled payment, or a payment of the debt in full, has been received by Her Majesty` `the day it was received`)
        (`cr1 seat: a day if it has happened` `the debt or part of it has been remitted under subsection 66(3) of the Act` `the day it was remitted`)
        (`cr1 seat: a day if it has happened` `the penalty was reduced or the decision imposing it rescinded under subsection 90.1(4) of the Act` `the day it was reduced or rescinded`)
        (`cr1 seat: a day if it has happened` `there is a decision on the penalty by the Minister under subsection 81(2), or on an appeal or judicial review` `the day of the latest of those decisions`)
        (`cr1 seat: a day if it has happened` `the accrued interest has been remitted under subsection 87(7)` `the day the interest was remitted`)
        (`cr1 seat: a day if it has happened` `the debtor has died` `the day the debtor died`)

@export May the Minister remit the interest I owe (reg 87(7))?
GIVEN `the interest has ceased to accrue in accordance with paragraph 87(6)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the interest ceased to accrue in accordance with regulation 87(6)(c)?
      `the interest cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the interest not be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future?
      `the administrative costs of collecting the interest would exceed the amount of the interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the administrative costs of collecting the interest exceed the amount of that interest?
      `paying the interest would cause me undue hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would paying the interest result in undue hardship to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Minister remit the interest I owe` IF
    `reg 87(7) — the Minister may remit the interest in whole or in part` `the interest has ceased to accrue in accordance with paragraph 87(6)(c)` `the interest cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future` `the administrative costs of collecting the interest would exceed the amount of the interest` `paying the interest would cause me undue hardship`


§§ `H. My Social Insurance Number (reg 88)`

@export Can a Social Insurance Number be assigned to me (reg 88(1))?
GIVEN `I have already been assigned a Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already been assigned a Social Insurance Number?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a Social Insurance Number be assigned to me` IF
    `reg 88(1) — a Minister may cause a Social Insurance Number to be assigned to the individual` `I have already been assigned a Social Insurance Number`

@export Can a Social Insurance Number Card be issued to me (reg 88(2))?
GIVEN `a Social Insurance Number was caused to be assigned to me under subsection 88(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a Social Insurance Number caused to be assigned to you under regulation 88(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a Social Insurance Number Card be issued to me` IF
    `reg 88(2) — a Minister may cause a Social Insurance Number Card to be issued to the individual` `a Social Insurance Number was caused to be assigned to me under subsection 88(1)`


§§ `I. Which remittances the Regulations cover (Related Provisions)`

@export Do the Regulations apply to the amount that was required to be remitted on this day (SOR/97-472, s 4)?
GIVEN `the day by which the amount or contribution was required to be remitted to the Receiver General` IS A DATE @desc By what day was the amount or contribution required to be remitted to the Receiver General?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the Regulations apply to the amount that was required to be remitted on this day` IF
    `Related provision SOR/97-472, s 4 — the Regulations apply to the amount or contribution` `the day by which the amount or contribution was required to be remitted to the Receiver General`

@export Do subsections 27(1) and (2) of S.C. 2015, c. 36 apply to the amount that was required to be remitted on this day (2015, c. 36, s 27(3))?
GIVEN `the day by which the amount or contribution was required to be remitted to the Receiver General` IS A DATE @desc By what day was the amount or contribution required to be remitted to the Receiver General?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do subsections 27(1) and (2) of 2015 chapter 36 apply to the amount that was required to be remitted on this day` IF
    `Related provision 2015, c. 36, s 27(3) — subsections (1) and (2) apply to the amount or contribution` `the day by which the amount or contribution was required to be remitted to the Receiver General`

